BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aixdesign-kb-national-library-ai-exhibition-2026@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20260804T131913Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260831
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260901
SUMMARY:Deadline: AIxDESIGN x KB: Open Call for Sessions\, (Art)works and P
 erformances
DESCRIPTION:AIxDESIGN and the KB (Koninklijke Bibliotheek\, the National Li
 brary of the Netherlands) are building an exhibition and public programme 
 about AI\, made from the national collection\, at the KB in The Hague. Nad
 ia Piet is Creative Lead with the AIxDESIGN community\, co-presented with 
 the KB. The premise: long before neural nets\, libraries were the machines
  we built to organise human knowledge\, and the show uses the KB's collect
 ion to look at what AI is\, where it comes from\, and how it connects to t
 he older story of how we store\, sort\, and search what we know. Part of t
 he show lives in the KB Atelier\, with talks\, workshops\, and screenings 
 alongside\, intended as AI literacy you can wander into. WHAT THEY WANT: w
 ork that engages AI in some way (critical\, creative\, hands-on\, or playf
 ul)\; bonus if it also speaks to archives\, libraries\, or how we store an
 d sort knowledge\, though you do not need to touch the KB's collection to 
 take part. You may pitch to more than one track: (A) SOMETHING FOR THE OPE
 NING NIGHT\, a performance\, talk\, screening\, tour\, ritual\, booth\, ga
 me\, or other experience for the November 2026 opening\, fee EUR 1\,500 to
  2\,000\; (B) A SESSION IN THE EVENTS PROGRAMME\, a workshop or other sess
 ion once during the three-month run\, around 2.5 to 4 hours\, fee EUR 2\,0
 00 to 2\,500\; (C) AN (ART)WORK FOR THE EXHIBITION\, existing work in any 
 format (installation\, sculpture\, zine stand\, a corner of your own) stur
 dy enough for a public area with daily traffic\, honorarium EUR 200 to 400
  including licensing and production\; (D) SOMETHING ELSE ENTIRELY\, pitch 
 it anyway. WHO: artists\, designers\, researchers\, technologists\, perfor
 mers\, musicians\, archivists\, or educators working around AI\, data\, li
 braries\, or cultural heritage\; no finished idea or polished CV needed\, 
 just a clear\, specific pitch. You can be based anywhere and they especial
 ly welcome people outside the Netherlands\; the show is in-person in The H
 ague and the fee stays the same wherever you are coming from. HOW TO APPLY
 : send a short pitch through the form (which track\, your idea in a paragr
 aph or two\, roughly what it would need\, and a link to your work)\; takes
  about five minutes\, no full application required. Deadline: end of Augus
 t 2026. Questions to hello@aixdesign.co.\n\nOrganisation: AIxDESIGN\, co-p
 resented with the Koninklijke Bibliotheek (KB)\, National Library of the N
 etherlands\nLocation: KB\, The Hague\, Netherlands (in-person exhibition a
 nd programme)\; pitches welcome from people based anywhere\nAward: Fees by
  track: opening-night experience EUR 1\,500 to 2\,000\; a session in the e
 vents programme EUR 2\,000 to 2\,500\; an existing (art)work for the exhib
 ition EUR 200 to 400 honorarium (including licensing and production). The 
 fee stays the same wherever you are based.\nDuration: Exhibition runs Nove
 mber 2026 to February 2027\; opening event November 2026\n\nMore: https://
 nadiapiet.notion.site/Open-Call-AIxDESIGN-x-KB-Sessions-Art-works-More-38f
 37d0038338102b128c57cbeb16d2d?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_me
 dium=referral
URL:https://nadiapiet.notion.site/Open-Call-AIxDESIGN-x-KB-Sessions-Art-wor
 ks-More-38f37d0038338102b128c57cbeb16d2d?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrant
 desk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:KB\, The Hague\, Netherlands (in-person exhibition and programme)\
 ; pitches welcome from people based anywhere
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:waag-trust-me-im-an-airtist-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260804T131913Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: Trust me\, I'm an AI/rtist: Open Call for Creative Interv
 entions
DESCRIPTION:Waag Futurelab invites artists\, theatre makers\, choreographer
 s\, dancers\, game designers and other creative practitioners to engage di
 rectly with seven experimental generative AI Enablers being co-created wit
 h technologists and dance\, theatre and gaming professionals. The call is 
 an invitation into the development process: selected artists get access to
  the technologies\, datasets\, interfaces and assumptions that shape these
  systems while they are still being built. Rather than testing whether the
  systems work\, artists are asked to interrogate why they work the way the
 y do\, who they are designed for\, what forms of creativity they enable or
  constrain\, and what assumptions about culture\, intelligence\, authorshi
 p\, labour\, bodies\, audiences and society are embedded in them. Waag is 
 looking for individuals and collectives willing to move beyond adoption in
 to investigation\, and welcomes proposals that are speculative\, critical\
 , poetic\, provocative\, humorous\, performative\, constructive or disrupt
 ive\, including work that challenges\, misuses\, reimagines\, hacks\, subv
 erts or plays with the tools\, exposes hidden biases\, questions environme
 ntal costs\, or imagines alternative technological futures. THE SEVEN AI E
 NABLERS\, each requiring an on-site visit to its technology partner: the G
 eneric Procedural Content Generation Enabler (text-to-3D assets and avatar
 s\, CERTH\, Greece)\; the Data-Driven Cultural Content Adaptation Enabler 
 (audience-aware creative content ideation with ranked candidate ideas\, CE
 RTH\, Greece)\; the Cross-Domain Audience Engagement Analytics Enabler (tu
 rning heterogeneous cultural participation data into interpretable engagem
 ent signals\, The Audience Agency\, Warrington\, UK)\; the Dance Style Ana
 lysis and Generation Enabler (dance video into virtual 3D choreography\, d
 issected into body\, effort\, shape and space components\, Centre of Excel
 lence for Research & Innovation\, Cyprus)\; the Immersive Design Integrati
 on Enabler for Dance & Theatre (NLP-driven XR environments with speech-to-
 3D scene editing\, Cyprus)\; the Music-to-Movement Translation Enabler (au
 dio into a time-aligned feature set spanning genre classification\, emotio
 nal valence-arousal analysis\, rhythm extraction and latent-space projecti
 on\, feeding motion generation\, spatial audio and visual choreography\, A
 ristotle University of Thessaloniki\, Greece)\; and the Adaptive Narrative
  Enabler for Games & Theatre (an evolutionary AI trained on creator-writte
 n story elements that generates infinite story variations\, explicitly rej
 ecting LLMs because of their dependence on copyrighted or public-domain co
 rpora that encode 19th and early 20th century sexism\, racism and imperial
 ism\, CAUSA Creation\, Austria). ELIGIBILITY: artists\, designers\, creati
 ve technologists\, theatre makers\, dancers\, choreographers and game desi
 gners\, as individuals or collectives\; applicants must hold a European VA
 T number. An info session with live demonstrations of the AI Enablers runs
  31 July 2026\, 10:00 to 11:30 CEST (meeting ID 995 7016 2341). Applicatio
 ns go through Homerun using the official Application Template\, uploaded a
 s a PDF\; read the Guide for Applicants\, which contains the full Enabler 
 descriptions\, before applying. Questions: zoenie at waag dot org. The AI 
 Enablers and this call are part of the Horizon Europe project HAMLET\, whi
 ch aims to make generative AI accessible to cultural organisations of all 
 sizes. Closes 30 September 2026\, 23:59 CEST. Free to apply.\n\nOrganisati
 on: Waag Futurelab (Horizon Europe project HAMLET)\nLocation: Europe. Enga
 ging with a specific AI Enabler includes an on-site visit to its technolog
 y partner: CERTH (Greece)\, The Audience Agency (Warrington\, UK)\, the Ce
 ntre of Excellence for Research & Innovation (Cyprus)\, Aristotle Universi
 ty of Thessaloniki (Greece)\, or CAUSA Creation (Austria). Final presentat
 ions September 2027.\nAward: EUR 20\,000 commission fee excluding VAT\, in
 clusive of artist fee\, travel\, accommodation and production costs. Appli
 cants must have a VAT number in Europe. No application fee.\nDuration: Jan
 uary to September 2027\, with final presentations in September 2027\n\nMor
 e: https://waag.org/en/article/open-call-creative-interventions-trust-me-i
 m-airtist/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://waag.org/en/article/open-call-creative-interventions-trust-me-i
 m-airtist/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Europe. Engaging with a specific AI Enabler includes an on-site vi
 sit to its technology partner: CERTH (Greece)\, The Audience Agency (Warri
 ngton\, UK)\, the Centre of Excellence for Research & Innovation (Cyprus)\
 , Aristotle University of Thessaloniki (Greece)\, or CAUSA Creation (Austr
 ia). Final presentations September 2027.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:hva-digital-life-researcher-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260804T131913Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260730
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260731
SUMMARY:Deadline: Amsterdam University of Applied Sciences: Digital Life Re
 searcher (Embodied AI Rehabilitation Agents)
DESCRIPTION:A junior researcher post in the Digital Life research group at 
 the Amsterdam University of Applied Sciences\, working on embodied AI reha
 bilitation agents that support patients during rehabilitation and recovery
  in everyday life. The programme sits at the intersection of human-centred
  AI\, digital health and rehabilitation technology\, and the role is unusu
 ally hands-on for a research job: co-designing rehabilitation technologies
  with patients and healthcare professionals\, building interactive prototy
 pes with sensing technologies and embodied interaction\, running user-cent
 red evaluations in real-world living lab settings\, and contributing to sc
 ientific reports and presentations. REQUIREMENTS: a master's degree in hum
 an-computer interaction\, industrial design\, computer science\, software 
 engineering\, AI or a related field\; demonstrated research experience inc
 luding co-design and evaluation with diverse stakeholders\; experience des
 igning interactive prototypes with sensing or embodied systems\; sensor da
 ta collection\, processing and analysis skills\; and programming in Python
 \, JavaScript or comparable languages. Excellent written and spoken Englis
 h is required and Dutch proficiency is preferred. Apply with a CV and moti
 vation letter through the application portal. Contact: Bin Yu (b.yu@hva.nl
 \, 0638347028) or vacatures@hva.nl. Closes 30 July 2026.\n\nOrganisation: 
 Amsterdam University of Applied Sciences (Hogeschool van Amsterdam)\nLocat
 ion: Amsterdam\, Netherlands (Weesperzijde campus)\, on site\nAward: EUR 3
 \,064.08 to 4\,084.93 gross per month for 40 hours per week\, plus an 8.3 
 percent year-end bonus and 8 percent holiday allowance.\nDuration: Full-ti
 me\, 40 hours per week\n\nMore: https://www.academictransfer.com/en/jobs/3
 62580/digital-life-onderzoeksmedewerker-researcher/?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.academictransfer.com/en/jobs/362580/digital-life-onderzoeks
 medewerker-researcher/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=re
 ferral
LOCATION:Amsterdam\, Netherlands (Weesperzijde campus)\, on site
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:twente-postdoc-conversational-ai-cultural-heritage-2026@artificialnouve
 au.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260804T131913Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260816
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260817
SUMMARY:Deadline: University of Twente: Postdoc\, Multimodal Conversational
  AI for Cultural Heritage
DESCRIPTION:A postdoctoral position in the Human Media Interaction group at
  the University of Twente on the project 'Balancing Personalisation and Po
 lyvocality: Dialogic Interaction for Open-mindedness and Empathy in Conver
 sational AI'. The work develops and evaluates multimodal conversational ag
 ents for museum settings that hold personalisation in tension with exposur
 e to plural perspectives\, rather than optimising for engagement alone. Ta
 sks include building models that use gaze\, speech and dialogue data to in
 fer visitor engagement and openness\, designing adaptive dialogue strategi
 es\, running VR-based user studies\, and publishing in strong venues. Of t
 he current Dutch academic postings this is the closest thing to a funded c
 reative-technologist brief: museum interpretation\, multimodal sensing and
  dialogue design in one role. REQUIREMENTS: a PhD in computer science\, AI
 \, HCI or a related field\; experience with conversational AI\, dialogue s
 ystems or adaptive systems\; experience running empirical research\, prefe
 rably user studies\; strong analytical and academic writing skills\; and e
 xcellent English. Apply with a CV including publications\, a motivation le
 tter and two academic references. Contact: Shenghui Wang (shenghui.wang@ut
 wente.nl). NOTE: the AcademicTransfer listing page shows a 16 August 2026 
 deadline while the detail page states 17 August 2026\, so treat 16 August 
 as the effective cut-off.\n\nOrganisation: University of Twente\, Human Me
 dia Interaction group\nLocation: Enschede\, Netherlands\nAward: EUR 3\,546
  to 5\,538 gross per month for 40 hours per week (8 salary steps\, dependi
 ng on experience)\, plus standard Dutch university holiday and year-end al
 lowances.\nDuration: One year\, renewable for a further two years subject 
 to positive evaluation\; 40 hours per week\n\nMore: https://www.academictr
 ansfer.com/en/jobs/362707/postdoc-position-on-multimodal-conversational-ai
 -for-cultural-heritage/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=r
 eferral
URL:https://www.academictransfer.com/en/jobs/362707/postdoc-position-on-mul
 timodal-conversational-ai-for-cultural-heritage/?utm_source=artificialnouv
 eaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Enschede\, Netherlands
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:twente-postdoc-llms4eu-ethics-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260804T131913Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260825
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260826
SUMMARY:Deadline: University of Twente: Postdoc\, Ethics and Epistemology o
 f LLMs4EU (17 months)
DESCRIPTION:A postdoctoral position in the Philosophy section at the Univer
 sity of Twente\, part of the 4TU.Center for Ethics and Technology\, workin
 g on the ethics and epistemology strand (Work Package 6) of LLMs4EU. LLMs4
 EU is a European Commission funded initiative led by the Alliance for Lang
 uage Technologies\, spanning more than 20 countries\, to build large langu
 age models across all EU languages and preserve European linguistic and cu
 ltural diversity in the digital age while keeping the resulting tools comp
 liant with European values and legislation including the AI Act and the GD
 PR. TASKS: establish benchmarking frameworks that address legal and ethica
 l concerns\; develop guidelines for fine-tuning processes with an emphasis
  on preserving cultural heritage\; oversee ethics compliance and advise th
 e project ethics board\; and build frameworks that integrate ethical consi
 derations into LLM design. This is the tech-communication and language-pol
 itics end of AI research rather than a modelling job: the questions are wh
 ose language\, whose culture and whose norms get encoded when a continent 
 builds its own models. REQUIREMENTS: a doctorate in ethics\, philosophy\, 
 science and technology studies\, AI ethics\, computer science with an ethi
 cs focus\, or a related field\; demonstrated expertise in AI ethics and et
 hics compliance\; understanding of AI tool design and LLM development\; ap
 preciation for cultural diversity\; strong communication and organisationa
 l skills\; and professional English. Apply through the AcademicTransfer po
 sting. Closes 25 August 2026.\n\nOrganisation: University of Twente\, Phil
 osophy section / 4TU.Center for Ethics and Technology\nLocation: Enschede\
 , Netherlands\nAward: EUR 4\,241 to 5\,538 gross per month (scale 10\, ste
 ps 4 to 12) at 1.0 FTE\, plus 8 percent holiday allowance and an 8.3 perce
 nt year-end bonus.\nDuration: 17 months\, full-time (38 to 40 hours per we
 ek)\, with possible extension\n\nMore: https://www.academictransfer.com/en
 /jobs/362444/postdoctoral-researcher-17-months-ethics-and-epistemology-of-
 llms4eu-design-data-and-deployment/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&
 utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.academictransfer.com/en/jobs/362444/postdoctoral-researcher
 -17-months-ethics-and-epistemology-of-llms4eu-design-data-and-deployment/?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Enschede\, Netherlands
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
